    "reason": "[ev-bc2d5eccce0f] lists only the new per-rule fields. It never says what \"These\" refers to, so the subject being replaced is not named, and it doesn't say whether that subject is deprecated or removed. The CRD diffs ([ev-236984661abb], [ev-272f02d3e90d], [ev-d4e55a3c3ecb], [ev-af63781cf017]) only prove that these per-rule fields were added in 1.13.0. They show no field being removed or deprecated, so they can't establish the change type, who is exposed or what happens to existing policies. The item also bundles five separate field replacements. The missing piece is the text just before L634 in the same blog section, which should name the replaced settings and state their deprecation or removal status and what happens if an operator does nothing.",
